igest":"sha256:86d9a6b50e58aca89e306f9430d91a70d440e178d17694bd7f081be19bd3fcd8","downloadCount":0,"id":"RA_kwDOVPcXOs4ndq2N","label":"","name":"up-term-src.lha","size":111820689,"state":"uploaded","updatedAt":"2026-10-21T10:09:10Z","url":"https://github.com/spotUP/vtcon/releases/download/v1.5/up-term-src.lha"},{"apiUrl":"https://api.github.com/repos/spotUP/vtcon/releases/assets/662089106","contentType":"application/x-lzh-compressed","createdAt":"2026-10-21T10:08:29Z","digest":"sha256:7814dbd16ece0d38d6b67e902a972eece7384202922e843c4c735bf45d4ef6e0","downloadCount":2,"id":"RA_kwDOVPcXOs4ndq2S","label":"","name":"up-term.lha","size":27696902,"state":"uploaded","updatedAt":"2026-10-21T10:08:51Z","url":"https://github.com/spotUP/vtcon/releases/download/v1.5/up-term.lha"},{"apiUrl":"https://api.github.com/repos/spotUP/vtcon/releases/assets/662089799","contentType":"application/vnd.shana.informed.package","createdAt":"2026-10-21T10:08:46Z","digest":"sha256:8a1c2ab78e070f11dfcc5ef9b11dabb1ab9c120f3a28b41f421c796c1fc9b197","downloadCount":0,"id":"RA_kwDOVPcXOs4ndrBH","label":"","name":"up-vim_1.0_m68k-amigaos.ipk","size":3592748,"state":"uploaded","updatedAt":"2026-10-21T10:08:49Z","url":"https://github.com/spotUP/vtcon/releases/download/v1.5/up-vim_1.0_m68k-amigaos.ipk"},{"apiUrl":"https://api.github.com/repos/spotUP/vtcon/releases/assets/662088991","contentType":"text/plain; charset=utf-8","createdAt":"2026-10-21T10:08:27Z","digest":"sha256:9f815276b2ba4beb933052d8d7eb220dea62928c330fb4b939cfd2419b59a543","downloadCount":1,"id":"RA_kwDOVPcXOs4ndq0f","label":"","name":"upkg-index.txt","size":622,"state":"uploaded","updatedAt":"2026-10-21T10:08:27Z","url":"https://github.com/spotUP/vtcon/releases/download/v1.5/upkg-index.txt"}],"body":"UP-Term 1.5 fixes two screen faults that 1.4 users saw in `upkg browse` and in a new shell window.\n\nOnly the base (up-term.lha) changes in this release. The add-ons keep their 1.3 versions.\n\n## Fixes\n\n- `upkg browse` (and any other full-screen program that draws a box first) no longer shows the UP-Term logo of the shell screen over its list on the first paint. On an AGA window, a frame that fell back to drawing in place skipped every blank cell, so the old screen stayed under it.\n- The tutorial hint of a new shell window fits in 80 columns. It is two lines now, not one line that broke in the middle of a word.\n\n## Install\n\nYou need a 68020 or better and AmigaOS 3.0 or newer. upkg downloads over the network: it needs a TCP/IP stack (Roadshow, Miami or AmiTCP) and AmiSSL 5, and the curl option ticked in Install.\n\nNew install:\n\n1. Download `up-term.lha` from the assets below and unpack it with lha.\n2. Double-click `Install` in the UP-Term drawer. Tick the optional parts you want, curl among them. Without Installer, use the Shell route in the kit's README.txt.\n3. Reboot after Install. XCON: and PTY: are mounted from then on.\n4. Open an UP-Term window and run `upkg update`, then `upkg browse`.\n\nUpgrade from 1.3 or 1.4: unpack the 1.5 `up-term.lha` and run its `Install`. The first page names the installed version and offers Update (the default). Update copies only the files that changed and keeps your choices and your add-ons. `upkg` is part of the base, so a new version of it always comes with up-term.lha, never as an ipk.\n\n## Add-ons (upkg feed)\n\nThese ipk packages are in this release's feed (`Packages`, `Packages.gz`). They keep their 1.3 versions.\n\n| Add-on | Version | Contents |\n|---|---|---|\n| up-claude | 1.1 | Claude Code for the Amiga (C:Claude) |\n| up-pi | 1.0 | amiga-pi, the pi coding agent |\n| up-nvim | 1.0 | Neovim 0.12 in UP-Term:nvim |\n| up-python | 1.0 | Python 3.14 in SYS:Python3 |\n| up-git | 1.0 | git 2.56.0 |\n| up-perl | 1.0 | Perl 5.42.3 |\n| up-vim | 1.0 | Vim 9.2.1202 |\n\nWithout the list:\n\n```\nupkg update                 fetch the feed's package list\nupkg list                   the packages the feed offers\nupkg list-installed         the add-ons you have\nupkg info <name>            details of one add-on\nupkg install <name>         install an add-on\nupkg upgrade                bring the installed add-ons up to the feed\nupkg remove <name>          remove an add-on\nupkg --help                 all commands\n```\n\nThe .lha archives of up-claude, up-pi, up-nvim and up-python are also here. Use them to install those add-ons without upkg.\n\n## Assets\n\n- `up-term.lha`: the base kit, version 1.5.\n- `*.ipk`, `Packages`, `Packages.gz`: the add-on feed that upkg reads.\n- `upkg-index.txt`: the index of the .lha archives.\n- `up-claude.lha`, `up-pi.lha`, `up-nvim.lha`, `up-python.lha`: stand-alone archives.\n- `up-term-src.lha`: the source of the base.\n\nBuilt from spotUP/UP-Term de8d662d, upterm 0208b9c. The kit's VERSIONS file lists the commit of each repository.\n","createdAt":"2026-10-19T10:56:28Z","name":"UP-Term 1.5","tagName":"v1.5","targetCommitish":"main"}
